{
  "$comment": [
    "Gate 9 registry of dynamic t() calls: every t(<not a string literal>) in src/ must be listed here.",
    "Read by scripts/find-missing-i18n-keys.mjs. Every string a listed source holds is a used key and must exist in all ten src/locales/*.json files.",
    "sites: { \"<file>\": { \"<argument as written, whitespace collapsed>\": [\"<source id>\", ...] } }. For t(a ?? b) or t(c ? a : b) each dynamic side is its own entry; string-literal sides need none.",
    "sources: { \"<id>\": { \"file\", and one of: \"name\" (a const, or a function whose literal return values are the keys), \"type\" (string-literal union members), \"calls\" + \"arg\" (literals passed to that function) } }.",
    "  Optional: \"props\" (only strings under these property names), \"take\": \"keys\" (object property names, not values), \"transform\": \"capitalize\", \"format\": [\"prefix.{}.suffix\"] (keys built from each value).",
    "  { \"runtime\": \"<reason>\" } declares a value that is not a fixed set of keys (text the caller already translated, AI or user text, a raw value shown as a last resort). Say why.",
    "Vocabulary sources (vocab-*) cover runtime values drawn from the app's shared lists (subjects, classes, boards, languages).",
    "The gate fails on an unlisted dynamic call, a site that no longer matches the code, a source it cannot read, and a source no site uses.",
    "An entry may be { \"sources\": [...], \"count\": N } when N calls in the file share the same argument text; a plain list covers exactly one call. The count is pinned so a new call reading the same (often generic) expression must be checked and declared, not ride on the first call's entry."
  ],
